y simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions:  \n\n- Region I is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region II is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region III is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region IV is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains a hole.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-98690/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1af47ea-6253-5d58-9b94-31e52de27106"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98690"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-98682/selection/9b75d957cb2d38823b17465e66061317515cbadec606145e6f59818de5a7b7de" :answer/id #uuid "452dfbd6-0883-5e4c-a175-ceab41fea21b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/848cf1a33161ac9fb25282cadc2f469675198a69b1df4a04d5eb88c15f66ebcc.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98682/selection/f37d183475094205ecb774913b9adb30e5caa277584bd9a99